ntelligence and steal the nation's military and atomic secrets. Over the course of the next decade, he and young FBI supervisor Bob Lamphere worked together on Venona, a top-secret mission to uncover the Soviet agents and protect the Holy Grail of Cold War espionage--the atomic bomb. Opposites in nearly every way, Lamphere and Gardner relentlessly followed a trail of clues that helped them identify and take down these Soviet agents one by one, including Julius and Ethel Rosenberg. But at the center of this spy ring, seemingly beyond the American agents' grasp, was the mysterious master spy who pulled the strings of the KGB's extensive campaign, dubbed Operation Enormoz by Russian Intelligence headquarters. Lamphere and Gardner began to suspect that a mole buried deep in the American intelligence community was feeding Moscow Center information on Venona. They raced to unmask the traitor and prevent the Soviets from fulfilling Soviet Premier Nikita Khrushchev's threat: \"We shall bury you!\"","publicationYear":2018,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Intelligence officers","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-in-the-enemy-s-house-the-secret-saga-of-the-fbi-agent-and-the-code-breaker-who-caught-the-russia"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"United States. Federal Bureau of Investigation","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-in-the-enemy-s-house-the-secret-saga-of-the-fbi-agent-and-the-code-breaker-who-caught-the-russia"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"United States","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-in-the-enemy-s-house-the-secret-saga-of-the-fbi-agent-and-the-code-breaker-who-caught-the-russia"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-in-the-enemy-s-house-the-secret-saga-of-the-fbi-agent-and-the-code-breaker-who-caught-the-russia"},{"source":"open_library","scheme"